            {
              "_key": "c2l1-006",
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "Mini and micro contracts exist for a reason. Gold Mini has exactly the same price as Gold but one-tenth the quantity, so every rupee of price movement means one-tenth the profit or loss. For beginners, the right contract is usually the smallest one that expresses your view."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-007",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-007s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Tick Size and Tick Value",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-008",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008m1",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The smallest price movement a futures contract can make, such as ₹1 for gold or ₹0.10 for natural gas."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008m2",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The rupee profit or loss on one lot when the price moves by one tick."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "tick size",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-008m1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008s3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " is the smallest price movement the contract allows. The ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008s4",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "tick value",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-008m2"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-008s5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " is what that one tick is worth to you in rupees, on one lot.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-009",
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{Tick value} = \\text{Tick size} \\times \\frac{\\text{Lot size}}{\\text{Quotation unit}}",
              "caption": "Make sure lot size and quotation unit are in the same units, for example both in grams."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-010",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-010s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Gold: ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-010s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹1 × (1,000 grams ÷ 10 grams) = ₹1 × 100 = ₹100 per tick",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-011",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-011s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Gold Mini: ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-011s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹1 × (100 grams ÷ 10 grams) = ₹1 × 10 = ₹10 per tick",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-012",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-012s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Natural Gas: ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-012s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "₹0.10 × (1,250 mmBtu ÷ 1 mmBtu) = ₹125 per tick",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-013",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-013s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Once you know the tick value, profit and loss is simple:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-014",
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{P\\&L} = \\text{Price change in ticks} \\times \\text{Tick value} \\times \\text{Number of lots}",
              "caption": "Equivalently: price change × (lot size ÷ quotation unit) × number of lots."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-015",
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "numericInput",
              "title": "Copper tick value",
              "prompt": "MCX Copper has a lot size of 2,500 kg, is quoted in ₹ per kg, and has a tick size of ₹0.05. What is the tick value of one lot, in rupees?",
              "correctValue": 125,
              "tolerance": 0,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "₹0.05 × (2,500 kg ÷ 1 kg) = ₹125. A move from ₹900.00 to ₹905.00 per kg is 100 ticks, worth ₹12,500 on one lot."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-016",
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Which tick hurts most?",
              "question": "Which of these contracts has the highest tick value per lot?",
              "options": [
                "Gold (₹1 tick, 1 kg lot, quoted per 10 grams)",
                "Crude Oil Mini (₹1 tick, 10 barrel lot)",
                "Silver (₹1 tick, 30 kg lot)",
                "Natural Gas (₹0.10 tick, 1,250 mmBtu lot)"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 3,
              "explanation": "Gold = ₹100, Crude Oil Mini = ₹10, Silver = ₹30, Natural Gas = ₹125. A small-looking tick size of ₹0.10 can still carry the highest rupee value when the lot is large."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-017",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-017s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Contract Value: What You Are Really Controlling",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-018",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-018m1",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The full rupee value of the commodity covered by one futures lot, also called notional value. Your profit or loss is based on this, not on the margin you post."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-018s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-018s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "contract value",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-018m1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-018s3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ", or notional value, is the full rupee value of the commodity one lot represents.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-019",
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{Contract value} = \\text{Price} \\times \\frac{\\text{Lot size}}{\\text{Quotation unit}}",
              "caption": "Multiply by the number of lots for the total position size."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-020",
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-020s1",
                  "label": "Gold at ₹1,00,000 per 10 g",
                  "value": "₹1,00,00,000",
                  "context": "One 1 kg lot = ₹1 crore"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-020s2",
                  "label": "Gold Mini at ₹1,00,000 per 10 g",
                  "value": "₹10,00,000",
                  "context": "One 100 gram lot"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-020s3",
                  "label": "Silver at ₹1,20,000 per kg",
                  "value": "₹36,00,000",
                  "context": "One 30 kg lot"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-020s4",
                  "label": "Crude Oil at ₹6,500 per barrel",
                  "value": "₹6,50,000",
                  "context": "One 100 barrel lot"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-021",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-021s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "These prices are illustrative. The point is the scale: even the \"small\" Crude Oil contract represents ₹6.5 lakh of crude, and a full Gold lot represents ₹1 crore of gold.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-022",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-022s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Margin: Why You Do Not Pay the Full Value",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-023",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023m1",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The amount the exchange requires you to deposit before taking a futures position, calculated to cover a large one-day loss. On MCX it is based mainly on SPAN margin plus an extreme loss margin."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023m2",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "Standard Portfolio Analysis of Risk: a system that estimates the worst likely one-day loss on a position across many price and volatility scenarios."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "You do not pay the contract value upfront. Instead, you deposit ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "initial margin",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-023m1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023s3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ", a fraction of the contract value set by the exchange's clearing corporation to cover a large one-day loss. On MCX, this is calculated mainly as ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023s4",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "SPAN margin",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-023m2"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-023s5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " plus an extreme loss margin, and the exchange can add extra margins when volatility jumps.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-024",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-024m1",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "Controlling a position much larger than the cash you put down, so that gains and losses are magnified relative to your capital."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-024s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Margin is not a cost or a fee. It is a good faith deposit that stays yours, but it is also the first thing losses eat into. Because you control a big position with a small deposit, futures are ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-024s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "leveraged",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-024m1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-024s3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-025",
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\text{Leverage} = \\frac{\\text{Contract value}}{\\text{Margin}} = \\frac{1}{\\text{Margin \\%}}",
              "caption": "A price move of exactly the margin percentage wipes out the entire margin."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-033",
              "_type": "collapsible",
              "title": "Show me the math: 8% margin on one Gold lot",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-026",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-026s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Assume Gold is at ₹1,00,000 per 10 grams and total margin is 8% of contract value. The 8% is illustrative; actual margins vary by commodity and change with volatility.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-027",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1,
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-027s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Contract value: ₹1,00,00,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-028",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1,
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-028s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Margin: 8% × ₹1,00,00,000 = ₹8,00,000",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-029",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1,
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-029s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Leverage: 1 ÷ 0.08 = 12.5 times",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-030",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1,
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-030s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "If gold falls 2% (₹2,000 per 10 grams): loss = ₹2,000 × 100 = ₹2,00,000, which is 25% of your margin",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-031",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "listItem": "bullet",
                  "level": 1,
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-031s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "If gold falls 8%: loss = ₹8,00,000, your entire margin",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-032",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "markDefs": [],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "c2l1-032s1",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "A 2% move in gold is an ordinary week. On a fully margined position, it is a quarter of your capital.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-034",
              "_type": "chart",
              "chartType": "bar",
              "title": "Share of margin lost for a 2% adverse price move",
              "xAxisLabel": "Margin as % of contract value",
              "yAxisLabel": "% of margin lost",
              "data": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-034d1",
                  "label": "5%",
