                  "_key": "c2l1-043s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Expiry: Every Contract Has an End Date",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-044",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-044m1",
                  "_type": "glossaryTerm",
                  "definition": "The last day a futures contract trades. After that, open positions are settled in cash or through physical delivery, depending on the contract."
                }
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-044s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Unlike a share, a futures contract does not last forever. Each contract has an ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-044s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "expiry date",
                  "marks": [
                    "c2l1-044m1"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-044s3",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " after which it stops trading and settles. MCX lists several contract months for each commodity at the same time, and the exchange publishes a calendar of expiry dates.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-045",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-045s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Monthly or bi-monthly. ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-045s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Some contracts, like Crude Oil and Gold Mini, have a new contract every month. The full 1 kg Gold contract is listed for alternate months.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-046",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-046s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Expiry dates are linked to underlying markets. ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-046s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Crude Oil contracts, for example, expire close to the expiry of the related NYMEX WTI contract, usually around the third week of the month.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-047",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-047s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Near, next and far months. ",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c2l1-047s2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The nearest expiry is usually the most liquid. Traders who want to hold a view longer close the near contract and open the next one, which is called rolling over.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c2l1-048",
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "warning",
              "text": "Some MCX contracts, including gold and silver, can settle by physical delivery, and they enter a tender or delivery period in the days before expiry, with much higher margins. If you are a speculator with no intention of taking or giving delivery, know these dates and close or roll your position before they begin. The next lesson covers settlement in detail."
            },
